{"questions":[{"question_id":"KxDI6IEJbr7AahXR","paperTitle":"AIEEE 2004","year":2004,"examDate":2004,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"chemical-bonding-and-molecular-structure","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","topic":"hybridization-and-vsepr-theory","type":"mcq","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"the-states-of-hybridization-of-boron-and-oxygen-atoms-in-bor-2004-marks-4-kxdi6iejbr7aahxr.htm","content":"The states of hybridization of boron and oxygen atoms in boric acid (H<sub>3</sub>BO<sub>3</sub>) are respectively ","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"sp<sup>2</sup> and sp<sup>2</sup>\n "},{"identifier":"B","content":"sp<sup>3</sup> and sp<sup>3</sup>"},{"identifier":"C","content":"sp<sup>3</sup> and sp<sup>2</sup>"},{"identifier":"D","content":"sp<sup>2</sup> and sp<sup>3</sup>\n "}],"correct_options":["D"],"explanation":"Structure of&nbsp; H<sub>3</sub>BO<sub>3</sub>&nbsp; is \n<br><br><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/MpXboC47va8PNuleV/W3PQy78F9NqAapXxu66VFmzMmeyK1/eIgFKZvt9n0dkZoF3ClgH4/image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%;  height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"AIEEE 2004 Chemistry - Chemical Bonding &amp; Molecular Structure Question 258 English Explanation\">\n<br><br>Here Boron has 3 sigma bond. So it is sp<sup>2</sup> hybridised. \n<br><br>And oxygen has  two sigma bond and two lone pair. So it sp<sup>3</sup> hybridised."}]}